# CLI reference

Full reference for `{{ module_name }}-cli` and shell commands provided by the devshell.

## Global options

```bash
{{ module_name }}-cli [options] <subcommand>

  -E, --env          Deployment environment (Local, Test, Development, Staging, Production)
  -c, --config-root  Config directory (default: config/)
  -s, --secrets-path Secrets file path
  -o, --override     Override config values: -o key.path=value
  -D, --debug        Enable debug mode (SQL logging, post-mortem debugger)
```

## Subcommands

| Command       | Purpose                                                            |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `web serve`   | Start a web app in production mode                                 |
| `web develop` | Start a web app with live-reload + remote debugger                 |
| `schema`      | Database migration commands (up, down, current, history, generate) |
| `script`      | Utility scripts                                                    |

## Shell commands

These are provided by the Nix devshell (available after `direnv allow`):

| Command                | Purpose                                           |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `stack-up`             | Start all dev services via process-compose        |
| `generate-api-clients` | Generate TypeScript API clients from OpenAPI spec |
| `install-hooks`        | Install pre-commit hooks                          |

## Common workflows

```bash
# Start everything for local dev
stack-up

# Backend only (no frontend)
{{ module_name }}-cli web develop <app>

# Override a config value for one command
{{ module_name }}-cli -o storage.postgresql.port=5433 schema up head

# Debug mode with SQL logging
{{ module_name }}-cli -D web develop <app>

# Run a utility script
{{ module_name }}-cli script <name>
```

## Schema subcommands

```bash
{{ module_name }}-cli schema current              # Show current migration
{{ module_name }}-cli schema up head              # Apply all pending migrations
{{ module_name }}-cli schema down -1              # Rollback one migration
{{ module_name }}-cli schema generate "add table" # Create a new migration
{{ module_name }}-cli schema history              # View migration history
```

## API client generation

```bash
# Automatic (starts/stops server as needed)
generate-api-clients <app>

# Use --force to skip dirty-file check
generate-api-clients <app> --force
```

If the server is already running (via `stack-up`), it will use the running instance.
